<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria to offer 20 bln levs 4-wk T-bills Dec 16.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria to offer 20 bln levs 4-wk T-bills Dec 16.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry will offer 20 billion levs of four-week floater coupon T-bills at an auction on Monday, the central bank (BNB) said.</p>
<p>The issue will be offered with no minimum acceptable price set in advance by the ministry.</p>
<p>The coupon equals the BNB's central interest rate (CIR) for the period to maturity. The CIR is now set at 15 percent monthly, or 180 percent annually.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow:</p>
<p> Issue number	 BG 3021696029</p>
<p> Auction date	 December 16, 1996</p>
<p> Issue date	   December 18, 1996</p>
<p> Maturity date	January 15, 1997</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
